## Session start
- Do NOT read any _context file at session start. Read one only when I ask about it, or when
  a task needs it (facts -> reference.md; status -> progress.md; before writing to a file;
  at session wrap).

## Files
- _context/progress.md   current status.  Read on demand.
- _context/todo.md       idea inbox.      Read on demand.
- _context/reference.md  durable facts.   Read on demand.
- _context/on-demand/journal.md  append-only history. Read ONLY when you need past
                                 decisions; append to it after significant work.
- _context/on-demand/notes.md    scratch that must survive to next session. Read ONLY when
                                 resuming the work it belongs to; near-empty at session start.
- input/   read-only. I drop files here; read on demand. Never write, move, rename or delete
           here, and never auto-read it at session start.
- output/  your deliverables.
Each _context file's header states its own purpose, update trigger and budget. Follow it.

## Writing
- Future intent -> todo.md.  Current truth -> progress.md (overwrite; no dated history blocks).
  Past event + why -> journal.md (append).  Durable fact -> reference.md.  Scratch -> notes.md.
- Every fact has ONE home. progress.md and todo.md may only POINT to it, never copy the body.
- Say so briefly when you write to one, e.g. "(noted to todo)".

## output/
- New deliverable -> <name>_v1.ext. Revision -> highest existing _vN + 1, unless I say to edit
  the latest in place, in which case edit that file and don't bump.
- Flat by default; group a deliverable's versions in output/<name>/ if I ask.

## Session wrap - before ending a session with meaningful work, or before compacting
1. Append this session's entry to journal.md (what / why / outcome).
2. Prune progress.md back to its skeleton.
3. Collapse resolved todos to one line + a journal date pointer; move to Archive.
4. Drain notes.md: route each item to its home, or delete it.
5. Check each _context file against the budget in its own header; compact anything over.

## Safety
Never send, publish, delete or share anything without confirming first. Prefer drafts.

